  },
  {
    question: 'Is there a file size limit?',
    answer: 'We recommend files under 500MB for best performance. The hard limit is 2GB due to browser memory constraints. Larger files may cause browser slowdown.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Are my videos uploaded to a server?',
    answer: 'No. All processing happens entirely in your browser using Web Workers and the Canvas API. Your video files never leave your device.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between the three extraction modes?',
    answer: 'Manual lets you scrub the timeline and capture exact frames. Auto Interval extracts frames at regular time intervals (e.g., every 1 second). Smart Scene Detection analyzes the video and extracts only keyframes where the scene changes, ideal for presentations and screen recordings.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Which export format should I choose?',
    answer: 'PNG for lossless quality (largest files). JPG for good quality with smaller files (70-95% quality). WebP for excellent web compression (70-95%). AVIF for best modern compression (50-80%) but requires Safari 16.4+, Chrome 85+, or Firefox 93+.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I extract frames from a specific time range?',
